From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: G81EM1 bring-up <g81em1@localhost>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wificond: demote malformed MTK scan entry log

The legacy MT6580 nl80211 driver returns two BSS dump entries without a BSSID
on each otherwise successful scan. ParseScanResult already rejects only those
entries and continues processing every valid result, so logging each rejection
as an error creates misleading recurring noise. Keep the diagnostic at debug
level without changing scan behavior.
---
 scanning/scan_utils.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scanning/scan_utils.cpp b/scanning/scan_utils.cpp
index 28fe206..d771ce2 100644
--- a/scanning/scan_utils.cpp
+++ b/scanning/scan_utils.cpp
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@ bool ScanUtils::ParseScanResult(unique_ptr<const NL80211Packet> packet,
   if (packet->GetAttribute(NL80211_ATTR_BSS, &bss)) {
     vector<uint8_t> bssid;
     if (!bss.GetAttributeValue(NL80211_BSS_BSSID, &bssid)) {
-      LOG(ERROR) << "Failed to get BSSID from scan result packet";
+      LOG(DEBUG) << "Failed to get BSSID from scan result packet";
       return false;
     }
     uint32_t freq;
-- 
2.43.0
